From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:19:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 146/155] domainset: a name and a suffix of one key are one
 key, as in sing v0.9.7

sing v0.9.7 (sing-box 1.14.3) compacts the sorted keys of domain.NewMatcher:
a name and a suffix that make the same key (a name that begins with "\n" or
"\r", as no domain does) are one key now, where sing used to stop the
process. The trie builds them the same way instead of refusing them, and so
does the build of sorted keys (the legacy way of rule sets of version 1, a
list with a name that is not valid UTF-8), which read past the end of the
second copy.

That build refuses an empty suffix now, as the trie does where sing stops
the process; so does NewSet before it hands a list with a name that is not
valid UTF-8 to sing.
